Date: Sat, 28 Nov 2026 18:51:04 +1100
Subject: [PATCH 1/3] Outcrop beside a second wall is placed; outcrop slivers
 are warned of; the guide says both

- A ladder band outcropping through one wall, next to a corner, carves a
  cavity that also reaches the other wall. That was refused ("only a one-band
  outcrop is built"). It is now placed under the gap rule an interior band
  beside a wall follows (0.3 wall cells to the second wall).
- Where an outcropping band meets the wall, a cell's smallest angle depends on
  where the band crosses the wall relative to the wall's vertices; measured on
  an annulus it falls below 1 degree between depths a tenth of a cell apart.
  place_fault_ribbon_2d warns below 5 degrees (computed over the ranks, printed
  once) and records info['outcrop_min_angle']. Moving the trace's top by
  0.1-0.4 of a cell cleared 33 of the 43 measured cases below 5 degrees.
- faults-in-convection.md: a section on a band near the surface (the interior
  gap rule, the outcrop warning, the cap meshing the fault's last segment).

test_0907 (tier B): the corner outcrop is placed, both walls labelled, the
corner vertex kept; the warning is printed exactly when the recorded angle is
below the limit, a sliver-prone outcrop records less than a clean one, and an
interior placement records none.

