+## A band near the surface
+
+`place_fault_ribbon_2d` places the band in one of two ways near a domain wall.
+
+- **Interior.** The band stops short of the wall. Its cavity may run along the wall,
+  so the band is placed when its skin is 0.3 wall cells or more from the wall. Closer
+  than that, the cells filled in between would be slivers (about 22 degrees at 0.3
+  wall cells, 1 degree at 0.01), and the placement is refused with the gap in cells and
+  both ways out: move the band further from the wall, or closer, so that it reaches the
+  wall as an outcrop. This holds on the gathered path (`seams="gather"`, the default).
+  The seam-conforming path still refuses a cavity that reaches the wall.
+- **Outcrop.** The band crosses the wall, and an unstructured cap carries it from its
+  last rung to the wall. Where the band meets the wall, a cell's smallest angle depends
+  on where the band crosses the wall relative to the wall's own vertices, and it can
+  drop below 1 degree between depths a tenth of a cell apart. The placement warns when
+  it is below 5 degrees and records it as `info["outcrop_min_angle"]`. Moving the
+  trace's top by 0.1-0.4 of a cell cleared about three cases in four on an annulus,
+  nearly all at dips of 20 degrees and more and about half at 10-15 degrees. When the
+  trace's top row lies in the cap, the cap's unstructured mesh also sets the fault's
+  nodes on that last segment.
+
 ## Cost and diagnostics
 
 - Through an overturn the nonlinear solve, not the multigrid, sets the cost: 15-25
